  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1)\nA weak cold front will cross the region early this morning as a \nclosed low pressure center tracks east through the lower Great Lakes\non today and Saturday. In its wake, temperatures over the Ohio \nValley will drop under northwest flow. Overnight temperatures will\ndrop to the low to mid 30s tonight, and a frost advisory has been\nissued. Tomorrow night will see readings dropping a little more,\nsolidly in the lower 30s with some upper 20s possible. \n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2)\nA dry forecast is expected after Friday through most of next week as\nnorthwest flow aloft becomes more westerly. Starting Monday, \ntemperatures will modify a little each day, generally in the low to \nmid 60s for highs and mid-upper 30s for lows. For Thursday and\nFriday, a l/w trough will cross the region, bringing temperatures\nback down to the 50s for highs and lower 30s for lows.",
